  "solution": {
    "text": "Complexes of the type <math><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><msub><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> show geometrical or fac-mer isomerism. (where, aa = bidentate ligand and a is monodentate ligand.) Among the given, dichlorodiglycinato cobalt (III), I.e., <math><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> is such salt, so it will show fac and mer isomerism.<br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/97192a27-19c0-46ca-a85e-8f662c9fab5c.jpeg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width:4.4in;height:1.69167in\" />",
